---
import VisaPage from '../../../components/ui/VisaPage.astro';
---
<VisaPage
  lang="en"
  title="Panama Rentista Retirado Visa — Fixed Deposit Residency"
  description="Complete guide to Panama's Rentista Retirado (Retired Annuitant) visa: fixed deposit requirements, Special Passport, no age minimum, 5-year temporary residency."
  visaName="Panama Rentista Retirado Visa"
  tag="Fixed deposit · No age limit"
  tagColor="bg-jade/15 text-jade font-semibold"
  mainReq="Fixed deposit in Panama state bank generating $850+/month interest"
  investment="Approx. $250,000 USD fixed deposit in Banco Nacional or Caja de Ahorros"
  processingTime="Approx. 6 months"
  renewalNote="5-year temporary residency · renewable · grants Special Passport directly"
  intro="Panama's Rentista Retirado visa — established under Law No. 9 of 1987 — offers a unique path to temporary residency through a fixed-term bank deposit in one of Panama's state banks. Unlike the Pensionado visa, there is no minimum age requirement and no need for a pension or employer. Unlike the Qualified Investor visa, the deposit is backed by the Panamanian state. A key benefit is that this visa grants the Special Panamanian Passport directly to the main applicant and dependents — providing visa-free access to more than 140 countries, including the entire Schengen Area and the United Kingdom."
  requirements={[
    "Fixed-term deposit (plazo fijo) at a Panamanian state bank — Banco Nacional de Panamá or Caja de Ahorros — generating a minimum monthly interest of $850 USD. At current rates, this typically requires approximately $250,000 USD in capital",
    "The deposit must be placed for a minimum term of 5 years and remains immobilized (cannot be withdrawn) during that period",
    "The deposit receives sovereign backing from the Panamanian state and is free from liens during the 5-year term",
    "Valid passport with at least 6 months of validity remaining, plus complete authenticated copies",
    "National criminal background check from your country of origin — apostilled, maximum 6 months old",
    "Apostilled civil documents: birth certificate; marriage certificate if including a spouse",
    "Bank certification of the fixed deposit and interest generated",
    "Medical exam performed in Panama",
    "Passport-size photos and payment of government fees",
    "All foreign documents must be apostilled or authenticated by the Panama Consulate and translated by an Authorized Public Translator in Panama"
  ]}
  benefits={[
    "5-year temporary residency, directly renewable — no need to re-qualify from scratch at renewal",
    "No minimum age requirement — available to any adult regardless of age or professional status",
    "No need for a pension, employer, or business activity in Panama",
    "The deposit is held in a Panamanian state bank with sovereign backing — capital is protected and free from liens during the 5-year term",
    "Special Panamanian Passport (Documento Especial de Viaje) granted directly to the main applicant and all dependents — visa-free or visa-on-arrival access to 140+ countries, including all 27 Schengen Area countries and the United Kingdom",
    "Spouse and children qualify as dependents on the same application",
    "Freedom to live in Panama, open bank accounts, and access local services during the residency period",
    "No Panama tax on foreign-source income — the deposit interest itself is your qualifying income"
  ]}
  notFor={[
    "You do not have approximately $250,000 USD in capital available to lock into a fixed deposit for 5 years",
    "You need to access your capital within 5 years — the deposit is immobilized for the full term",
    "You want permanent residency from day one — the Rentista Retirado starts as a 5-year temporary residency",
    "You need full unrestricted work authorization in Panama under formal employment — this visa has labor restrictions for formal employment (entrepreneurial activities are generally possible)",
    "You are seeking Panamanian citizenship on a shorter path — consider the Qualified Investor or Friendly Nations routes, which can lead to permanent residency and eventual citizenship"
  ]}
  faqs={[
    {
      q: "What is the Panama Rentista Retirado visa?",
      a: "The Rentista Retirado (Retired Annuitant) visa, established under Law No. 9 of 1987, grants temporary residency in Panama to individuals who place a fixed-term bank deposit in a Panamanian state bank generating at least $850 USD per month in interest. There is no age minimum, no pension required, and no need for employment or business activity in Panama. It is one of the most straightforward pathways to residency for anyone who has liquid capital and does not yet qualify for a pension-based or investment-based visa."
    },
    {
      q: "How much money do I need for the Panama Rentista Retirado visa?",
      a: "The required capital is the amount necessary to generate at least $850 USD per month in interest through a fixed-term deposit at Banco Nacional de Panamá or Caja de Ahorros. At current deposit rates, this typically requires approximately $250,000 USD. The exact amount needed depends on the interest rate offered by the state bank at the time of application — your immigration attorney can confirm the current rate and the resulting required capital."
    },
    {
      q: "Which banks are eligible for the Rentista Retirado deposit?",
      a: "The deposit must be placed exclusively at one of Panama's two state banks: Banco Nacional de Panamá or Caja de Ahorros. Deposits at private banks — even those regulated by the Superintendency of Banks of Panama — do not qualify for this visa. The state bank deposit receives sovereign backing from the Panamanian government and remains free from liens or encumbrances during the 5-year term."
    },
    {
      q: "Does the Rentista Retirado visa grant the Special Panamanian Passport?",
      a: "Yes — and this is one of the most distinctive benefits of this visa. The Rentista Retirado visa grants the Special Panamanian Passport (Documento Especial de Viaje) directly to the main applicant and to all qualifying dependents. This travel document provides visa-free or visa-on-arrival access to more than 140 countries, including all 27 countries in the Schengen Area (European Union) and the United Kingdom. It does not confer Panamanian nationality or voting rights — your original citizenship remains unchanged."
    },
    {
      q: "Is there a minimum age requirement for the Rentista Retirado visa?",
      a: "No. The Rentista Retirado visa has no minimum age requirement. Any adult — regardless of age, profession, or whether they are retired — can apply, as long as they meet the financial requirement. This makes it distinct from pension-based programs like the Pensionado visa, which requires a guaranteed lifetime pension."
    },
    {
      q: "Who can be included as a dependent on the Rentista Retirado visa?",
      a: "The following family members may be included: your spouse; children under 18 years of age; children between 18 and 25 years old who are single, enrolled as full-time students, and economically dependent; children of any age with an accredited disability; and the parents of the main applicant (with no age limit). All qualifying dependents also receive the Special Panamanian Passport directly — not as an option, but as part of the visa benefit."
    }
  ]}
/>
